[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-125432"] :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=-\\frac{2x}{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{2y}{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $F$ is conservative\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4xy}{(1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-125446/selection/655610c33f9ee70bd034b89a5aa2c6ed9461fb56dcb4fb9b8027be65bbde5b10" :answer/id #uuid "f2e7fbe4-8644-51cd-a6b7-d02403611fa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125446/selection/1a2c3881891ab7eca8aa4af8d7002d84b8252f633df18da1be453e64ebd8a8b4" :answer/id #uuid "f7d6aea2-5a91-570b-9f9c-5839795ff01c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125446/selection/ad963bcdf2fe034ec60767210e5b564fc417b3b8813d0edc4c20ea2f1c8c2358" :answer/id #uuid "311c39c5-0207-5287-8708-a95d5aaef05a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125446/selection/cd8957b3e03d9fbea87893281373eded912abde9aae6462917a9ce8659b8cc99" :answer/id #uuid "5cea2142-8bbb-5931-93ac-166d64e9c435" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125446/selection/7c07cb852d1d9d8f5c291070fae09ae7d988365e5d8d9e30f8cf9e144690b3ce" :answer/id #uuid "0958f585-b03a-5b71-a62c-b4179617c1e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125446/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8d51c7b-47fb-5169-bdf2-f5813239023c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125446/selection/1a2c3881891ab7eca8aa4af8d7002d84b8252f633df18da1be453e64ebd8a8b4" :answer-field/choices ["q-125446/selection/655610c33f9ee70bd034b89a5aa2c6ed9461fb56dcb4fb9b8027be65bbde5b10" "q-125446/selection/1a2c3881891ab7eca8aa4af8d7002d84b8252f633df18da1be453e64ebd8a8b4" "q-125446/selection/ad963bcdf2fe034ec60767210e5b564fc417b3b8813d0edc4c20ea2f1c8c2358" "q-125446/selection/cd8957b3e03d9fbea87893281373eded912abde9aae6462917a9ce8659b8cc99" "q-125446/selection/7c07cb852d1d9d8f5c291070fae09ae7d988365e5d8d9e30f8cf9e144690b3ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125446" :question/id #uuid "d6300f2a-0327-598a-96a2-018f646c39ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-125446" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=-y\\,i+x\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =-y\\,i+x\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =2{sin}^{2}⁡t+2{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =2(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =4\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125446/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "976e05d4-59a8-5a93-be2f-b22357f388b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125446"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125460/selection/1e92e7e13074920ac5aa882943c0d0cc16dd496cdd41b0ca0e7d7d1595497ada" :answer/id #uuid "f77e869d-ba44-56db-923a-6488b4c4df83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125460/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "654336de-2d6d-5292-bad6-f9e7b54fdcaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125460/selection/0fb978d2b1ce374ae0f1700c585078833e85991af693baf7445a5e2dc6cdf6cc" :answer/id #uuid "e83b69f4-4396-5458-961d-379c85eb8536" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125460/selection/b9e37961d17591920349894dfae8783436f581130d0da0bd042142640bfd4f67" :answer/id #uuid "d1fa8594-4785-53d0-92d0-5a0f78e75574" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125460/selection/3d7e9581eb340ca865781aadd66d3a388123ded67207e85e7c884876f49dbe1a" :answer/id #uuid "9e58365b-0782-5893-b776-dba3a1fc926b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125460/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1060da2b-be12-5fc6-9f02-223cf08e1535" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125460/selection/3d7e9581eb340ca865781aadd66d3a388123ded67207e85e7c884876f49dbe1a" :answer-field/choices ["q-125460/selection/1e92e7e13074920ac5aa882943c0d0cc16dd496cdd41b0ca0e7d7d1595497ada" "q-125460/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-125460/selection/0fb978d2b1ce374ae0f1700c585078833e85991af693baf7445a5e2dc6cdf6cc" "q-125460/selection/b9e37961d17591920349894dfae8783436f581130d0da0bd042142640bfd4f67" "q-125460/selection/3d7e9581eb340ca865781aadd66d3a388123ded67207e85e7c884876f49dbe1a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125460" :question/id #uuid "4ba67b8a-fb87-555b-9bbd-2816c5ef8c09" :question/math-academy-id "q-125460" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{5}{y}\\,i-\\frac{5}{x}\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{5}{y}\\,i-\\frac{5}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =5+5 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }10\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =10t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =10(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =20\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125460/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "976e05d4-59a8-5a93-be2f-b22357f388b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125460"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125651/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "d17e34dd-1ce7-54e0-85a9-a0fc42892bd3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125651/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "c4fc4c9e-4f88-55f5-bbc4-dc71193f19e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125651/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "f2df90bb-2666-5eed-9017-91597f06385e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125651/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" :answer/id #uuid "b922ee65-d59c-5ed4-9ff6-b0d55d177cde" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125651/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "8c793010-6ace-532a-97b7-3609c9ff9922" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125651/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d39bf09a-a54c-57c7-8c90-9a678e97c28f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125651/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" :answer-field/choices ["q-125651/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-125651/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-125651/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-125651/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" "q-125651/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125651" :question/id #uuid "3978b78e-e07e-5b8b-b056-7941114ea124" :question/math-academy-id "q-125651" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)=\\frac{{e}^{xy}}{{x}^{2}+1}$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $∇f$ is **not** conservative\n- ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n- ${∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0$ for some closed paths $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The vector field $∇f$ is conservative by definition.\n\n- Statement II is false. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\n- Statement III is false. The circulation $Γ=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125651/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1da220a9-2afc-5b63-a423-a4d2b3de9567"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125651"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125652/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "f2422945-9a64-5b99-83e9-a9ae52c7d96a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125652/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" :answer/id #uuid "f1d2e74d-0087-5ef3-b1ac-3e4db3c92229" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125652/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "693e305d-7f7d-5716-aa2b-238ba6d8c03b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125652/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "7340c3bd-9565-51ad-b7ee-b17c344b0ac7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125652/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "87a39776-06d3-520a-9e22-7e6e60169335" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125652/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2b92c4f-5dc3-5e2c-889e-8c690b5cbfb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125652/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-125652/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-125652/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" "q-125652/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-125652/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-125652/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125652" :question/id #uuid "99450b1c-b23d-5f38-be2e-6ef7f79586dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-125652" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)={5}^{-x-y}+\\sqrt{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $∇f$ is conservative\n- ${∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n- ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise linear path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The vector field $∇f$ is conservative by definition.\n\n- Statement II is false. The circulation $Γ=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125652/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1da220a9-2afc-5b63-a423-a4d2b3de9567"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125652"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
